---
title: Overview
description: How a contract is built from the services picked on an opportunity, approved, signed and filed.
sidebar:
  order: 1
---

Contracts are prepared on an opportunity in CRM. The person in charge picks the services on the opportunity, and Operon builds the contract from the firm's template: the scope and fee sections list exactly the services picked, at the agreed prices. A discounted contract goes to the department head for approval; the contract is then sent for e-signature or signed on paper. Every file of the deal stays with the opportunity.

## The stages of a contract

| Stage | What happens |
|---|---|
| **1 Prepare** | Choose the client, the signatory, the issuing entity, the language and the format. |
| **2 Draft** | Generate the contract and read it through. |
| **3 Approval** | Only when needed: a discount above the firm's threshold, or a draft edited by hand. |
| **4 Signing** | Send for e-signature, or sign on paper. |
| **5 Signed** | The signed copy is filed with the opportunity. |

## Who does what

| Role | Work |
|---|---|
| **Department head** | Keeps the department's services, packages, prices and contract wording up to date. Approves discounted contracts. |
| **Person in charge (PIC)** | Picks the services and prices on the opportunity, prepares and generates the contract, submits it and sends it for signing. |
| **Tenant admin** | Maintains the issuing entities and the contract settings. Approves a contract that a department head submitted. |

